Z||000000||Philphine||07-11-2000||02:50 AM||||<BR>since i'm having trouble with my fiero and also having got a replacement rear window for my truck (s10 blazer rear windows see lots of hard times) i've been driving my truck more. it has the biggest system i've put in a vehicle. the fiero seems a little weak now. it's made me start work on the 3 sub idea i've mentioned occasionaly before.<P>i have an 8 in the passenger footwell and i plan to put an 8 in each door. i'll need to switch to power windows and work out the enclosures. if it's like most projects this time next year i'll about have it almost worked out.<P>just thought i'd mention it.<P><BR>------------------<P><BR>'87 coupe (feral)<BR>'84 indy<p>[This message has been edited by Philphine (edited 07-11-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000001||KevinP||07-11-2000||02:28 PM||||Try out this idea....If you already have an 8 in the footwell and all your wires run, just uprade what you have.  I've had a 10 inch Eclipse in there and it is asolutely DEAFENING!  Cutting apart the doors sounds like kind of a hassle  me, I like my installs nice and easy. I'm puttig a 12" Cerwin-Vega in now, legroom suffers some, but some sacrifices need to be made.  Keep me posted with whatever you do.<BR>Later,<BR>Kevin<P>||||reg||3
Z||000002||Philphine||07-12-2000||02:38 AM||||my footwell enclosure is so small a 10 won't fit in it. if i could fit it in it probaly wouldn't have enough air. i have 8's in my blazer doors (for woofers though, not subs) and i think i have the idea worked out for the fiero. plus if it works it will be how i set up the indy (with out the footwell sub. thanks for the input though.<p>[This message has been edited by Philphine (edited 07-12-2000).]||||reg||1
